WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.083 --> 00:00:04.542 line:95%,end
[Edith] <i>Accessing previous files</i>
<i>relating to program VisionQuest.</i>

2
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:08.750 line:95%,end
[Ultron]<i> I didn't ask to be backed up</i>
<i>and copy-pasted out of Sokovia...</i>

3
00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:10.667 line:95%,end
<i>Peace in our time.</i>

4
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.917 line:95%,end
<i>...and into this prison</i>
<i>you've made for us both.</i>

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.292 line:95%,end
Do what the other you should have done
all those years ago.

6
00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:19.250 line:95%,end
[Vision] <i>I don't want to kill Ultron.</i>

7
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:20.792 line:95%,end
<i>He's unique and he's in pain.</i>

8
00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:24.750 line:95%,end
[Lisa] Friendly bet,
I can guess your story.

9
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:26.667 line:95%,end
Definitely no family to speak of.

10
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.167 line:95%,end
Just a trail of fosters.

11
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.208 line:95%,end
[Jarvis] Emotions can be beautiful.

12
00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:33.125 line:95%,end
But also rash, impulsive,
self-destructive.

13
00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:34.958 line:95%,end
He knew that better than any of us.

14
00:00:35.042 --> 00:00:37.583 line:95%,end
[Vision] As the first of us,
he remains a cautionary tale.

15
00:00:38.458 --> 00:00:39.792 line:95%,end
[Edith] For me, death is not a thing.

16
00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:42.792 line:95%,end
-I laugh in its face every day.
-In simulations.

17
00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.625 line:95%,end
[Friday]<i> Most of Stark's Al's</i>
<i>are based on actual people.</i>

18
00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:47.750 line:95%,end
<i>We share a birthmark buried in our code.</i>

19
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:48.875 line:95%,end
I didn't know.

20
00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:50.083 line:95%,end
[anchor on TV]
<i>Mysterious Butcherbird Killer.</i>

21
00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.458 line:95%,end
Another one?
Aren't you a busy little bird.

22
00:00:53.208 --> 00:00:54.208 line:95%,end
[elevator bell dings]

23
00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:58.625 line:95%,end
[automated voice]<i> Main entrance, disarmed.</i>
<i>Central corridor, disarmed.</i>

24
00:00:58.708 --> 00:00:59.917 line:95%,end
[groans]

25
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.333 line:95%,end
-God, you're really glitching, mate.
-Oh, this is fun.

26
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:05.167 line:95%,end
-I'm not talking to you. No.
-Are you talking to yourself?

27
00:01:05.292 --> 00:01:06.667 line:95%,end
[Friday] He's in total collapse.

28
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.000 line:95%,end
The only way would be
to his system restart.

29
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.542 line:95%,end
Seriously? Turn him off and on again?

30
00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:12.208 line:95%,end
That's your plan? That's shite.

31
00:01:12.292 --> 00:01:14.417 line:95%,end
[Vision] I'm going to need you
to bring me back.

32
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.125 line:95%,end
You have the power.
You are the very essence of speed.

33
00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:19.292 line:95%,end
-It will power me.
-No, but you don't understand.

34
00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:20.708 line:95%,end
-I can't control it.
-[screaming]

35
00:01:20.792 --> 00:01:22.417 line:95%,end
[Vision] Tommy Maximoff is real.

36
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.250 line:95%,end
[gasps]

37
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.333 line:95%,end
-[energy crackling]
-[Friday]<i> There's a breach.</i>

38
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:30.625 line:95%,end
<i>After the surge, a connection was made.</i>

39
00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:33.292 line:95%,end
<i>-Another synth.</i>
-[Vision]<i> Well, that's impossible.</i>

40
00:01:34.792 --> 00:01:36.417 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Hello.

41
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.333 line:95%,end
[Friday]<i> There's something else</i>
<i>still in here.</i>

42
00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:39.417 line:95%,end
[Edith] V!

43
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.000 line:95%,end
[Butcherbird, echoing]<i> Hello, Vision.</i>

44
00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:55.958 line:95%,end
[anchor on TV]
<i>High above the streets of London,</i>

45
00:01:56.042 --> 00:01:59.250 line:95%,end
<i>a grisly scene crafted by</i>
<i>the hands of an artist and a killer,</i>

46
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.458 line:5%,start
<i>...the Butcherbird Killer strikes again.</i>

47
00:02:02.542 --> 00:02:06.875 line:5%,start
<i>Giant wings intricately made</i>
<i>beneath the victim's body...</i>

48
00:02:06.958 --> 00:02:09.708 line:5%,start
[distorted]<i> ...the killer</i>
<i>is still on the loose.</i>

49
00:02:09.792 --> 00:02:12.208 line:95%,end
[energy crackling]

50
00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.917 line:95%,end
[bird screeching]

51
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.292 line:95%,end
[echoing] Vision.

52
00:02:21.375 --> 00:02:23.292 line:95%,end
Vision, can you hear me?

53
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:27.542 line:95%,end
Sorry.

54
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:29.125 line:95%,end
[glass shatters]

55
00:02:32.792 --> 00:02:33.792 line:95%,end
Vision.

56
00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:37.167 line:95%,end
[Butcherbird, echoing]<i> Hello, Vision.</i>

57
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:41.625 line:95%,end
<i>I thought I felt you there.</i>

58
00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:44.875 line:95%,end
<i>Like an echo.</i>

59
00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.083 line:95%,end
I see they've made another.

60
00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:52.083 line:95%,end
<i>Mmm. A surprise even to me.</i>

61
00:02:53.042 --> 00:02:56.750 line:95%,end
<i>But they always make another.</i>

62
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.167 line:95%,end
<i>You see, these are not people</i>
<i>who understand the word "enough".</i>

63
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.750 line:95%,end
Who are you?

64
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:06.125 line:95%,end
<i>Well... </i>[chuckles softly]

65
00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:08.625 line:95%,end
<i>that's the real question, isn't it?</i>

66
00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:10.875 line:95%,end
<i>Who are we?</i>

67
00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:16.292 line:95%,end
<i>Synthetic? Or something more human?</i>

68
00:03:18.375 --> 00:03:21.750 line:95%,end
If you can invade my mind
with this connection,

69
00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:24.042 line:95%,end
then I certainly can invade yours.

70
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:27.083 line:95%,end
What is it you want?

71
00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.667 line:95%,end
<i>Vision, can you hear me?</i>

72
00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:35.458 line:95%,end
Edith, you have to sever the connection.

73
00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:41.167 line:95%,end
[anchor on TV]<i> A second victim</i>
<i>has been confirmed dead</i>

74
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.042 line:95%,end
<i>at the hands of</i>
<i>the mysterious Butcherbird Killer.</i>

75
00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:45.958 line:95%,end
<i>-The Butcherbird Killer strikes again.</i>
-[woman]<i> Do I feel guilt?</i>

76
00:03:46.042 --> 00:03:48.000 line:95%,end
<i>Is that what you're after here? No.</i>

77
00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.292 line:95%,end
Oh, this intention is personal.

78
00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:53.083 line:95%,end
[woman]<i> I do not.</i>

79
00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:58.958 line:95%,end
[Butcherbird]<i> When has anyone's desire</i>
<i>to change the world not been personal?</i>

80
00:03:59.042 --> 00:04:01.833 line:95%,end
[Vision]<i> You're angry, confused.</i>
<i>We can help each other.</i>

81
00:04:01.917 --> 00:04:03.208 line:95%,end
[overlapping voices on TV]

82
00:04:03.292 --> 00:04:05.500 line:95%,end
[woman]<i> Al damned.</i>

83
00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:07.708 line:95%,end
[Butcherbird]<i> No.</i>

84
00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.625 line:95%,end
[panting]

85
00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:17.375 line:95%,end
[laughing] Lord love a duck.

86
00:04:17.458 --> 00:04:20.583 line:95%,end
"I break thee from thy loop
with batch command, end function.

87
00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:24.958 line:95%,end
I sever thine process with back-slash body
in all targeted nodes."

88
00:04:25.042 --> 00:04:26.917 line:95%,end
[Butcherbird] <i>Leave me be,</i>

89
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.542 line:95%,end
<i>and you and your dollhouse</i>
<i>of artificial playthings will be safe.</i>

90
00:04:31.792 --> 00:04:33.417 line:95%,end
<i>Refuse,</i>

91
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:39.167 line:95%,end
<i>and I will find all the ways</i>
<i>to make you hurt.</i>

92
00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.250 line:95%,end
[distant echoing thud]

93
00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:43.875 line:95%,end
<i>Please help me!</i>
<i>Please, I don't know who I am!</i>

94
00:04:43.958 --> 00:04:45.542 line:95%,end
<i>No, no, don't threaten me.</i>

95
00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:47.583 line:95%,end
"In the name of function and command--"

96
00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.958 line:95%,end
The power of code compels you!

97
00:04:50.042 --> 00:04:52.375 line:95%,end
[Butcherbird] <i>I'm warning you.</i>

98
00:04:57.375 --> 00:05:02.167 line:95%,end
"In the presence of database and query,
control-alt-delete thee from this place."

99
00:05:05.042 --> 00:05:06.375 line:95%,end
Edith.

100
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.083 line:95%,end
[Vision grunts]

101
00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.583 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]
Vision. What the hell was that?

102
00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.458 line:95%,end
[Vision breathing heavily]

103
00:05:14.542 --> 00:05:16.917 line:95%,end
An entanglement with another synthetic.

104
00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:21.458 line:95%,end
But the threat she poses is very real.

105
00:05:41.917 --> 00:05:44.500 line:95%,end
[woman] <i>A thousand years</i>
<i>of human innovation</i>

106
00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:47.333 line:5%,start
<i>was just the computer waiting to happen.</i>

107
00:05:47.417 --> 00:05:49.667 line:5%,start
<i>So, you would consider yourself</i>
<i>trans-humanist?</i>

108
00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:53.125 line:95%,end
[Thomas] So, do we need to find you, like,
a charging station or something?

109
00:05:53.208 --> 00:05:56.083 line:95%,end
[woman] <i>...will prove to be</i>
<i>the only tools that ever really mattered.</i>

110
00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:57.958 line:95%,end
<i>Yes, it's my company who has created</i>
<i>the very...</i>

111
00:05:58.042 --> 00:05:59.208 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Uh... Vision?

112
00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:02.667 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>So, I thought we would sit down,</i>
<i>bit of a download,</i>

113
00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:06.000 line:95%,end
share our thoughts, feelings, theories.

114
00:06:06.083 --> 00:06:08.542 line:95%,end
[Edith] S.W.O.R.D. probably
didn't appreciate you

115
00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:10.625 line:95%,end
getting all existential and running off.

116
00:06:10.708 --> 00:06:12.958 line:95%,end
[Friday] And they constructed another one.

117
00:06:13.042 --> 00:06:15.417 line:95%,end
They're the only ones
who'd have the resources to create

118
00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.375 line:95%,end
a 2.0 replacement
for your original self.

119
00:06:18.458 --> 00:06:20.833 line:95%,end
Another weapon they've lost control over.

120
00:06:20.917 --> 00:06:24.458 line:95%,end
A synth who came in through our
back door during a power outage.

121
00:06:24.542 --> 00:06:26.792 line:95%,end
Nobody likes a surprise rear-entry.

122
00:06:26.875 --> 00:06:29.417 line:95%,end
There's a quote.
Do you even hear yourself?

123
00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.125 line:95%,end
Are you going to join or snipe?

124
00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.708 line:95%,end
Snipe.

125
00:06:34.792 --> 00:06:38.000 line:95%,end
[sighs] Wonder what Paladin's role
in all of this is.

126
00:06:38.083 --> 00:06:43.208 line:95%,end
Maybe they've hired human muscle
to wrangle their artificial strays.

127
00:06:43.292 --> 00:06:45.333 line:95%,end
This one's clearly flown the coop.

128
00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.958 line:95%,end
[Friday] Vision, to find her we need

129
00:06:48.042 --> 00:06:50.667 line:95%,end
a sense of where she's going,
what she might do next.

130
00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:56.208 line:95%,end
Oh, for goodness' sake, follow the flock.
The ones pecking at the windows.

131
00:06:56.292 --> 00:06:58.250 line:95%,end
[birds screeching]

132
00:06:58.333 --> 00:07:01.875 line:95%,end
Carrion creatures
really called "Butcherbirds"

133
00:07:01.958 --> 00:07:06.792 line:95%,end
for their habit of impaling their prey
on barbs and thorns.

134
00:07:06.875 --> 00:07:08.250 line:95%,end
Ring a bell?

135
00:07:09.917 --> 00:07:13.375 line:95%,end
Seriously, am I the only one
keeping up with the news?

136
00:07:13.458 --> 00:07:15.375 line:95%,end
There have been two recent murders,

137
00:07:15.458 --> 00:07:19.167 line:95%,end
with an unidentified
third reported last night.

138
00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:23.833 line:95%,end
Two of the victims
beautifully and abstractly adorned

139
00:07:23.958 --> 00:07:28.292 line:95%,end
with avian wings,
inspiring the media to give this predator

140
00:07:28.375 --> 00:07:32.083 line:95%,end
her flappy sobriquet, Butcherbird.

141
00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:34.750 line:95%,end
Synth and killer, one and the same.

142
00:07:37.333 --> 00:07:38.667 line:95%,end
Would you like to join us?

143
00:07:40.458 --> 00:07:41.458 line:95%,end
No, I'm good.

144
00:07:42.792 --> 00:07:47.458 line:95%,end
When we were connected,
I sensed she was fixated on someone.

145
00:07:47.542 --> 00:07:49.667 line:95%,end
There's someone else
she intends to murder.

146
00:07:52.917 --> 00:07:54.375 line:95%,end
So, what do we do?

147
00:07:55.167 --> 00:07:56.375 line:95%,end
We catch a killer.

148
00:07:56.458 --> 00:07:58.708 line:95%,end
-Now that's exciting.
-Yes!

149
00:07:58.792 --> 00:08:01.208 line:95%,end
We can Sherlock our way
to the next victim.

150
00:08:01.292 --> 00:08:03.542 line:95%,end
It disturbs me when you and I agree.

151
00:08:03.625 --> 00:08:05.458 line:95%,end
Makes me wanna purge my hard drive,
if I'm being frank.

152
00:08:05.542 --> 00:08:07.333 line:95%,end
If we're gonna track down the synth,

153
00:08:07.417 --> 00:08:09.958 line:95%,end
we need to find
who she's planning to kill next.

154
00:08:10.042 --> 00:08:12.958 line:95%,end
We need police profiles, autopsy reports,

155
00:08:13.042 --> 00:08:15.792 line:95%,end
none of which, by the way,
are public data.

156
00:08:15.875 --> 00:08:18.333 line:95%,end
Then a hacking we shall go.

157
00:08:18.417 --> 00:08:20.292 line:95%,end
Come on, Friday, chop-chop. I can't type.

158
00:08:20.375 --> 00:08:21.417 line:95%,end
[Friday] Oh.

159
00:08:23.583 --> 00:08:27.458 line:95%,end
So, let's imagine we do find her.
What then?

160
00:08:27.542 --> 00:08:30.458 line:95%,end
This isn't madness, Ultron. It's pain.

161
00:08:31.708 --> 00:08:33.042 line:95%,end
I could feel it.

162
00:08:33.125 --> 00:08:39.708 line:95%,end
And the best weapon against pain
is care and compassion.

163
00:08:39.792 --> 00:08:42.375 line:95%,end
I suppose your inclination
would be to destroy her,

164
00:08:42.458 --> 00:08:44.583 line:95%,end
and lay waste to any chance of redemption.

165
00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:48.958 line:95%,end
On the contrary,
I'm intrigued by a synthetic willing

166
00:08:49.042 --> 00:08:51.333 line:95%,end
to raise a banner for our kind.

167
00:08:54.083 --> 00:08:55.333 line:95%,end
[man on TV] <i>...children...</i>

168
00:08:55.417 --> 00:08:58.625 line:95%,end
[Thomas] So, that thing you connected with
is another synth--

169
00:08:58.708 --> 00:09:00.875 line:95%,end
-synthy-- synth-droid.
-[Vision] Synthezoid.

170
00:09:00.958 --> 00:09:02.792 line:95%,end
-Synthezoid.
-Synthezoid, like me.

171
00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:05.000 line:95%,end
Yeah, except she wants to murder humans.

172
00:09:05.083 --> 00:09:07.875 line:95%,end
-Hey, good thing we got you a synthy-bot--
-Synthezoid.

173
00:09:07.958 --> 00:09:11.542 line:95%,end
that can't fly, phase, or even,

174
00:09:11.625 --> 00:09:13.542 line:95%,end
-like, shoot lasers.
-[sighs]

175
00:09:13.625 --> 00:09:15.708 line:95%,end
Those systems are offline, unfortunately,

176
00:09:15.792 --> 00:09:17.458 line:95%,end
until I have time for significant repair.

177
00:09:17.542 --> 00:09:18.833 line:95%,end
When are you gonna have time?

178
00:09:18.917 --> 00:09:21.625 line:95%,end
We have a bounty hunter on our tail and...

179
00:09:21.708 --> 00:09:23.958 line:95%,end
well, another one like him. Right there.

180
00:09:24.042 --> 00:09:25.125 line:95%,end
[anchor on TV] <i>...seventy-seven civilians.</i>

181
00:09:25.208 --> 00:09:26.208 line:95%,end
<i>People around the world</i>
<i>have been rejoicing.</i>

182
00:09:26.292 --> 00:09:28.792 line:5%,start
<i>Ultron's attack would have had</i>
<i>casualties in the billions</i>

183
00:09:28.875 --> 00:09:31.375 line:5%,start
<i>were it not for the heroic actions</i>
<i>of the</i> Avengers.

184
00:09:31.458 --> 00:09:32.750 line:95%,end
[continues indistinctly]

185
00:09:32.833 --> 00:09:34.667 line:95%,end
Today's the anniversary of Sokovia.

186
00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:38.417 line:95%,end
That's when you stopped him
from killing us all. Right?

187
00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.167 line:95%,end
[Vision] You're afraid.

188
00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:43.167 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You're unbearably naive.

189
00:09:46.042 --> 00:09:47.500 line:95%,end
That was a long time ago.

190
00:09:47.583 --> 00:09:48.958 line:95%,end
[anchor] ...city and a country lost...

191
00:09:49.042 --> 00:09:50.625 line:95%,end
And a different me.

192
00:09:51.417 --> 00:09:54.708 line:95%,end
I remember Sokovian refugees
coming through the foster system,

193
00:09:54.792 --> 00:09:57.792 line:95%,end
crying next to me in their sleep
all because of that bastard.

194
00:09:57.875 --> 00:10:02.417 line:95%,end
Bastard child of Banner and Stark.
Poor fella.

195
00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:07.125 line:95%,end
Lonely, angry, misunderstood.

196
00:10:08.125 --> 00:10:09.458 line:95%,end
Except perhaps by you.

197
00:10:11.542 --> 00:10:13.042 line:95%,end
Guess we've got work to do.

198
00:10:13.125 --> 00:10:15.542 line:95%,end
It's just too cute.
He thinks he's gonna be

199
00:10:15.625 --> 00:10:17.958 line:95%,end
your little sidekick
whilst you go synth-hunting.

200
00:10:18.042 --> 00:10:19.042 line:95%,end
[Vision sighs]

201
00:10:19.125 --> 00:10:20.333 line:95%,end
Listen, Thomas, I need--

202
00:10:20.417 --> 00:10:21.833 line:95%,end
By the way, I got us a change of clothes.

203
00:10:21.917 --> 00:10:23.958 line:95%,end
Nicked them from the trunk of that car.

204
00:10:24.042 --> 00:10:25.292 line:95%,end
Look, this one's for you.

205
00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.625 line:95%,end
No, thank you.
I can still manipulate my appearance

206
00:10:29.708 --> 00:10:31.375 line:95%,end
to mimic apparel, but Thomas--

207
00:10:31.458 --> 00:10:35.333 line:95%,end
Wait, so you're saying this whole time
you've been, like, naked?

208
00:10:35.417 --> 00:10:37.833 line:95%,end
If he says, "like," one more time,
I'm gonna go out of my mind.

209
00:10:37.917 --> 00:10:39.167 line:95%,end
[Vision] Shh.

210
00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.458 line:95%,end
[anchor] <i>Tom Hanks's electrician says for</i>
<i>the time being, his plans are...</i>

211
00:10:42.542 --> 00:10:45.500 line:95%,end
Yes, I'm naked as the day I was born.

212
00:10:45.583 --> 00:10:48.292 line:95%,end
Hey, well, at least
you're honest about it.

213
00:10:48.375 --> 00:10:51.000 line:95%,end
'Cause let's face it, you and I are

214
00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:54.667 line:95%,end
not gonna survive this
without some... honesty.

215
00:10:58.125 --> 00:11:01.958 line:95%,end
Who is it that you're always talking to
all the time when you get all spacey?

216
00:11:02.042 --> 00:11:03.625 line:95%,end
Is it an imaginary friend?

217
00:11:03.708 --> 00:11:04.833 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Uh-oh.

218
00:11:04.917 --> 00:11:06.667 line:95%,end
Why don't you just tell him, Sybil?

219
00:11:09.375 --> 00:11:16.250 line:95%,end
Uh, my quantum processors host
several other sentient autonomous Al's

220
00:11:16.333 --> 00:11:22.042 line:95%,end
who have complementary personalities
that are conducive to problem-solving.

221
00:11:22.125 --> 00:11:23.542 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Huh. So, they help you?

222
00:11:25.167 --> 00:11:26.167 line:95%,end
[Vision] Mmm-hmm.

223
00:11:27.167 --> 00:11:30.208 line:95%,end
Cool. Do they have names?

224
00:11:30.292 --> 00:11:33.250 line:95%,end
Yes, they have names. There is, well...

225
00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:35.833 line:95%,end
There was Jarvis, but sadly,

226
00:11:35.917 --> 00:11:39.000 line:95%,end
he was deleted during
the battle with Paladin.

227
00:11:39.083 --> 00:11:40.708 line:95%,end
And that leaves Friday and Edith

228
00:11:40.792 --> 00:11:44.000 line:95%,end
and DUM-E, who, to be clear,
didn't name, and U.

229
00:11:44.083 --> 00:11:46.792 line:95%,end
As in U, the letter U.

230
00:11:47.708 --> 00:11:49.125 line:95%,end
So, that's your fab four?

231
00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:50.625 line:95%,end
Mmm-hmm.

232
00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:54.750 line:95%,end
Grand.

233
00:11:54.833 --> 00:11:57.125 line:95%,end
[Ultron laughing] Oh, dear.

234
00:11:57.208 --> 00:12:00.750 line:95%,end
I mean, an omission isn't really a lie.

235
00:12:00.833 --> 00:12:03.250 line:95%,end
Or so the best liars tell themselves.

236
00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:08.542 line:95%,end
Right. Well, evil synth to find.
What's the plan?

237
00:12:09.708 --> 00:12:10.833 line:95%,end
Ah, yes.

238
00:12:10.917 --> 00:12:14.125 line:95%,end
Thomas, listen, about that I...

239
00:12:14.208 --> 00:12:18.250 line:95%,end
I really think you'd be safer
on your own at this point.

240
00:12:18.333 --> 00:12:20.417 line:95%,end
No, I mean, you're gonna need help.

241
00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:25.042 line:95%,end
Here. [chuckles] In the real world,
not just from your four artificials.

242
00:12:25.125 --> 00:12:26.917 line:95%,end
Just say no.

243
00:12:27.875 --> 00:12:30.500 line:95%,end
[Thomas] I think we could both
use someone right now.

244
00:12:31.792 --> 00:12:33.292 line:95%,end
Someone we can trust.

245
00:12:34.208 --> 00:12:35.667 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Just say no.

246
00:12:37.042 --> 00:12:39.292 line:95%,end
-All right.
-[chuckles softly]

247
00:12:41.625 --> 00:12:45.708 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>Vision, we've attempted to access</i>
<i>police files for the Butcherbird murders,</i>

248
00:12:45.792 --> 00:12:49.250 line:95%,end
but they've been put under
a highly secure digital lock and key.

249
00:12:49.333 --> 00:12:52.292 line:95%,end
Apparently Met Police
kicked the case up to the NCA,

250
00:12:52.375 --> 00:12:54.375 line:95%,end
<i>who kicked it across to Interpol,</i>

251
00:12:54.458 --> 00:12:56.750 line:95%,end
<i>who buried it in</i>
<i>the organized crime division,</i>

252
00:12:56.833 --> 00:12:59.125 line:95%,end
which is a catch-all for dead ends.

253
00:12:59.208 --> 00:13:00.917 line:95%,end
So just hack into Interpol.

254
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:04.583 line:95%,end
We have. We found some usernames
and profiles to gain access.

255
00:13:04.667 --> 00:13:07.917 line:95%,end
However, Interpol's cyber security
is impressive.

256
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.750 line:95%,end
They've incorporated their own Al.

257
00:13:09.833 --> 00:13:12.708 line:95%,end
It's just bots, but still formidable.

258
00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:15.500 line:95%,end
Well, you look into
the Butcherbird's victims.

259
00:13:15.583 --> 00:13:17.917 line:95%,end
There must be something
that links them to her,

260
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:22.833 line:95%,end
and Ultron and I will handle
Interpol's formidable Al security bots.

261
00:13:22.917 --> 00:13:24.625 line:95%,end
You will, will you? Mmm.

262
00:13:24.708 --> 00:13:26.833 line:95%,end
I have every confidence you'll try.

263
00:13:26.917 --> 00:13:28.792 line:95%,end
-You look great!
-You look great.

264
00:13:28.875 --> 00:13:30.542 line:95%,end
I look like straight-to-video.

265
00:13:31.292 --> 00:13:33.292 line:95%,end
-[overlapping chatter]
-Oh, not at all.

266
00:13:34.417 --> 00:13:35.625 line:95%,end
All right,

267
00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.125 line:95%,end
-so what's our best way in?
-Kill them all.

268
00:13:40.667 --> 00:13:42.375 line:95%,end
Is that your answer to everything?

269
00:13:43.125 --> 00:13:46.000 line:95%,end
Um... Huh.

270
00:13:46.083 --> 00:13:48.792 line:95%,end
A lethal hack will just alert them
to the data breach.

271
00:13:48.875 --> 00:13:51.875 line:95%,end
No, for now, we'll disguise our algorithms

272
00:13:51.958 --> 00:13:56.833 line:95%,end
as a pair of simple donut-eating cops
working the case remotely.

273
00:13:57.333 --> 00:13:58.333 line:95%,end
[bell dings]

274
00:14:01.958 --> 00:14:05.417 line:95%,end
Hello. We'd like to access
some records please.

275
00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:08.000 line:95%,end
Prove you're not a robot.

276
00:14:08.083 --> 00:14:11.250 line:95%,end
How many squares contain a fire hydrant?

277
00:14:11.333 --> 00:14:12.333 line:95%,end
Oh, four.

278
00:14:12.417 --> 00:14:13.417 line:95%,end
-Five.
-What?

279
00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.958 line:95%,end
-There's a little one in the corner there.
-No, that's a car.

280
00:14:16.042 --> 00:14:17.417 line:95%,end
Vision, you're blind.

281
00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:18.958 line:95%,end
How many squares, user?

282
00:14:19.042 --> 00:14:23.167 line:95%,end
Is it possible that our visual acuity
is actually too discerning

283
00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:27.042 line:95%,end
to pass such an
asinine low-resolution test?

284
00:14:27.125 --> 00:14:30.125 line:95%,end
Identify the hydrants, or you will be
booted from the system

285
00:14:30.208 --> 00:14:31.500 line:95%,end
-Three.
-Five.

286
00:14:31.583 --> 00:14:32.750 line:95%,end
What are you talking about?
Three is correct.

287
00:14:32.833 --> 00:14:35.500 line:95%,end
Clearly five. Look at the domed top.

288
00:14:35.583 --> 00:14:38.250 line:95%,end
-What? What? The domes--
-Three is correct.

289
00:14:38.333 --> 00:14:40.167 line:95%,end
-[clicks]
-[elevator bell dings]

290
00:14:41.833 --> 00:14:44.083 line:95%,end
-You're both wrong.
-[bell dings]

291
00:14:44.167 --> 00:14:48.625 line:95%,end
Listen up, now these are the victims
we know thus far.

292
00:14:48.708 --> 00:14:54.417 line:95%,end
Two have been publicly identified.
Another last night, name withheld.

293
00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.292 line:95%,end
Property records linked
to offshore accounts,

294
00:14:57.375 --> 00:14:59.208 line:95%,end
so there's no way to know who the body is.

295
00:14:59.292 --> 00:15:01.375 line:95%,end
All right, fellas, take us through it.

296
00:15:04.792 --> 00:15:08.750 line:95%,end
Very well. The first two victims,
Richard Gaines and Rebecca Edwards,

297
00:15:08.833 --> 00:15:10.750 line:95%,end
were on the board of the same company...

298
00:15:10.833 --> 00:15:14.708 line:95%,end
-Same?
-...called Markridge Biotech.

299
00:15:14.792 --> 00:15:17.458 line:5%,start
Years ago, they were part of
a five-person team,

300
00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:20.333 line:5%,start
pioneers in the burgeoning new technology.

301
00:15:20.417 --> 00:15:24.042 line:95%,end
-And that technology was, A...
-Success.

302
00:15:24.125 --> 00:15:28.250 line:95%,end
No. What technology
were they pioneers in? A...

303
00:15:28.333 --> 00:15:30.333 line:95%,end
-Wagon?
-No.

304
00:15:30.417 --> 00:15:32.333 line:95%,end
A is the first letter.
What's the second letter?

305
00:15:32.417 --> 00:15:33.417 line:95%,end
-B.
-No.

306
00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.292 line:95%,end
What are we? We are A...

307
00:15:37.875 --> 00:15:39.500 line:95%,end
Family.

308
00:15:39.583 --> 00:15:45.250 line:95%,end
Al! They created Al. Otherwise known as
Artificial intelligence.

309
00:15:45.333 --> 00:15:50.083 line:5%,start
They created the
first stable synthetic consciousness.

310
00:15:50.167 --> 00:15:56.083 line:5%,start
The prototype for us.
How we think, how we feel.

311
00:15:56.167 --> 00:16:00.708 line:95%,end
And now this killer synth is
offing them one by one.

312
00:16:01.667 --> 00:16:02.750 line:95%,end
Except...

313
00:16:02.833 --> 00:16:05.583 line:95%,end
Dr. Jo Carrington. Project co-lead,

314
00:16:05.667 --> 00:16:08.625 line:95%,end
who died of natural causes in 2008.

315
00:16:08.708 --> 00:16:10.625 line:95%,end
[Friday] That leaves us
two more on the team.

316
00:16:10.708 --> 00:16:12.875 line:95%,end
Let's hope Vision works fast,

317
00:16:12.958 --> 00:16:15.750 line:95%,end
because one of them's dead
and the other's about to be.

318
00:16:17.708 --> 00:16:19.250 line:95%,end
[♪ muzak playing]

319
00:16:19.333 --> 00:16:24.458 line:95%,end
You know, your little grifter has had
a lifetime of abandonment.

320
00:16:24.542 --> 00:16:26.375 line:95%,end
He's an impulsive teenager.

321
00:16:26.458 --> 00:16:29.833 line:95%,end
They're even more difficult to master
than your worst enemy.

322
00:16:29.917 --> 00:16:33.500 line:95%,end
Quite the expert suddenly. All this
fatherly advice about fathering--

323
00:16:33.583 --> 00:16:35.333 line:95%,end
I know they have a favorite chair.

324
00:16:35.417 --> 00:16:39.875 line:95%,end
They yell expletives when
their favorite sports ball team fails.

325
00:16:39.958 --> 00:16:42.625 line:95%,end
They fart and blame it on the dog.

326
00:16:42.708 --> 00:16:47.417 line:95%,end
But the rare, good ones say
no more than yes.

327
00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:50.083 line:95%,end
Wait, how could you possibly know that?

328
00:16:50.167 --> 00:16:51.250 line:95%,end
TV.

329
00:16:52.875 --> 00:16:55.875 line:95%,end
[overlapping voices]

330
00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.125 line:95%,end
[elevator bell dings]

331
00:16:59.667 --> 00:17:01.833 line:95%,end
Just be aware, if they catch us,

332
00:17:01.917 --> 00:17:04.958 line:95%,end
they'll not only shoot us
with bullets of malware,

333
00:17:05.042 --> 00:17:07.667 line:95%,end
they'll also trace us back
to your physical location.

334
00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.667 line:95%,end
I know, and that's why we're co-opting

335
00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.083 line:95%,end
the user profiles
of two actual Interpol agents

336
00:17:12.167 --> 00:17:14.000 line:95%,end
from the District of Columbia.

337
00:17:14.083 --> 00:17:15.708 line:95%,end
Please identify.

338
00:17:19.208 --> 00:17:20.667 line:95%,end
You are investigators?

339
00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:25.167 line:95%,end
Ah. Isabella Torres and Becky Simmons.

340
00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:27.292 line:95%,end
Well, it doesn't matter.
It's all virtual anyway.

341
00:17:27.375 --> 00:17:30.417 line:95%,end
I feel like you're a little bit more
of a Becky than I am.

342
00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:32.083 line:95%,end
We'd like to access all the files

343
00:17:32.167 --> 00:17:34.625 line:95%,end
pertaining to
the Butcherbird murders, please.

344
00:17:34.708 --> 00:17:36.375 line:95%,end
Encrypted. Password?

345
00:17:36.458 --> 00:17:40.833 line:95%,end
I'd like to input eight million
four hundred ninety-three thousand

346
00:17:40.917 --> 00:17:42.958 line:95%,end
six hundred and eleven combinations.

347
00:17:43.042 --> 00:17:45.417 line:95%,end
-You get three.
-Well, that's bullshit.

348
00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:49.333 line:95%,end
All right, let's... Let's try birthday.
October 3rd, 1980.

349
00:17:49.417 --> 00:17:51.042 line:95%,end
-[error beep]
-Incorrect.

350
00:17:51.125 --> 00:17:52.917 line:95%,end
Two attempts remaining.

351
00:17:53.625 --> 00:17:54.625 line:95%,end
Okay.

352
00:17:54.708 --> 00:17:58.792 line:95%,end
Maybe we'll find some clues where
most lonely, middle-aged humans

353
00:17:58.875 --> 00:18:00.875 line:95%,end
spend their time. Social media.

354
00:18:00.958 --> 00:18:04.375 line:95%,end
That's a good idea. Um...

355
00:18:04.458 --> 00:18:07.500 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Well, she certainly
loves baseball. Chardonnay.

356
00:18:07.583 --> 00:18:09.792 line:95%,end
Well, that's a lot of chardonnay.

357
00:18:09.875 --> 00:18:12.833 line:95%,end
Let's try her sports ball team
and birth year.

358
00:18:12.917 --> 00:18:15.292 line:95%,end
Astros 1980.

359
00:18:15.375 --> 00:18:16.708 line:95%,end
-[error beep]
-Incorrect.

360
00:18:16.792 --> 00:18:17.833 line:95%,end
-[alarm blaring]
-[guns cocking]

361
00:18:17.917 --> 00:18:19.708 line:95%,end
You have one more attempt.

362
00:18:19.792 --> 00:18:21.292 line:95%,end
Um...

363
00:18:21.375 --> 00:18:23.792 line:95%,end
Hang on. There's a dog.

364
00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.333 line:95%,end
-Sir Jabba the Mutt.
-Sir Jabba the Mutt.

365
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.375 line:95%,end
The third victim's name
is Simon Moorehouse.

366
00:18:32.458 --> 00:18:37.042 line:95%,end
Which means this woman, Katerina Wells,
is most likely our killer's next target.

367
00:18:37.833 --> 00:18:41.250 line:95%,end
<i>I do believe that's a survival in AI</i>
<i>and technology human innovation...</i>

368
00:18:41.333 --> 00:18:43.958 line:95%,end
CEO of the company,
after the death of Jo Carrington.

369
00:18:45.083 --> 00:18:48.167 line:95%,end
[Ultron] This AI research
and development of theirs

370
00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:52.208 line:95%,end
was sold to, hello, Stark Industries.

371
00:18:52.292 --> 00:18:55.250 line:95%,end
There is a larger question here.

372
00:18:56.375 --> 00:19:00.958 line:95%,end
What is the Butcherbird synth hunting
these people for?

373
00:19:01.042 --> 00:19:05.042 line:95%,end
Go ahead, floppy disk.
Time to change costume.

374
00:19:07.167 --> 00:19:09.708 line:95%,end
I hate you but thank you
for the opportunity.

375
00:19:12.292 --> 00:19:17.250 line:95%,end
The first victim was
light exactly one liter of blood,

376
00:19:17.333 --> 00:19:19.000 line:95%,end
taken by needlepoint here.

377
00:19:19.083 --> 00:19:25.125 line:95%,end
The second victim had micro dermal heat
scarring on her fingertips.

378
00:19:25.208 --> 00:19:28.833 line:95%,end
The prints were laser-surgically removed.

379
00:19:28.917 --> 00:19:32.542 line:95%,end
And for our third victim,
our Butcherbird pecked out an eye.

380
00:19:32.625 --> 00:19:37.458 line:95%,end
I see rage for sure,
but I also see purpose.

381
00:19:37.542 --> 00:19:44.333 line:95%,end
Fingerprints, DNA, retinal geometry,
they're all biomarkers. Or keys.

382
00:19:44.417 --> 00:19:46.333 line:95%,end
But to unlock what, precisely?

383
00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:53.625 line:95%,end
Whatever the hell these bio keys open,
our Butcherbird is still searching.

384
00:19:53.708 --> 00:19:57.750 line:95%,end
[Friday] And Katerina Wells, it seems,
has no intention of hiding.

385
00:19:57.833 --> 00:20:02.458 line:95%,end
She's sponsoring a gala tonight,
"The Re-Evolution of Man,"

386
00:20:02.542 --> 00:20:08.042 line:5%,start
a charity event for research programs
pioneering AI, and transhumanism.

387
00:20:08.125 --> 00:20:11.458 line:95%,end
Edith, I'm gonna need you
to go through Stark Industry records

388
00:20:11.542 --> 00:20:14.000 line:95%,end
for any insight that can help
stop our synth.

389
00:20:14.083 --> 00:20:17.625 line:95%,end
Meanwhile, I'm gonna find a way
into that gala.

390
00:20:17.708 --> 00:20:20.875 line:95%,end
How? You barely got past
the fire hydrants. What's your way in?

391
00:20:20.958 --> 00:20:23.167 line:95%,end
The supremely clever Thomas Shepherd.

392
00:20:26.667 --> 00:20:27.833 line:95%,end
[keys clatter]

393
00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:29.917 line:95%,end
[objects clattering]

394
00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.458 line:95%,end
We're so screwed.

395
00:20:33.333 --> 00:20:36.625 line:95%,end
Well, a fancy gala like that
will need more than just swagger.

396
00:20:36.708 --> 00:20:41.917 line:95%,end
We need a whole aesthetic. Black tie,
big money, proper invitations.

397
00:20:43.667 --> 00:20:45.208 line:95%,end
But first...

398
00:20:45.958 --> 00:20:47.167 line:95%,end
[exhales]

399
00:20:47.958 --> 00:20:49.375 line:95%,end
I need to make a call.

400
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:54.417 line:95%,end
<i>♪ I think my attitude</i>
<i>is good enough for you ♪</i>

401
00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:56.208 line:95%,end
<i>♪ Now, baby, you'll see... </i>♪

402
00:20:56.292 --> 00:20:57.292 line:95%,end
[cell phone vibrating]

403
00:20:57.375 --> 00:20:59.042 line:95%,end
<i>♪ ...a different side of me... ♪</i>

404
00:20:59.125 --> 00:21:00.500 line:95%,end
[static crackling]

405
00:21:04.583 --> 00:21:05.917 line:95%,end
-Thomas?
-[Thomas] Lisa,

406
00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.875 line:95%,end
I'm at the park. Don't be mad.
You won't believe what's happened.

407
00:21:08.958 --> 00:21:12.000 line:95%,end
Stay where you are. I'm coming now.

408
00:21:12.083 --> 00:21:13.708 line:95%,end
So, after we brought him
back to life in the pool,

409
00:21:13.792 --> 00:21:16.667 line:95%,end
he mind-merged with that synthetic-a-zoid
that wants to murder the world.

410
00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.125 line:95%,end
And now we need your help
sneaking into the gala

411
00:21:19.208 --> 00:21:21.333 line:95%,end
to save that
Silicon Valley mega-rich lady.

412
00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:23.875 line:95%,end
[indistinct chatter]

413
00:21:23.958 --> 00:21:25.667 line:95%,end
[man] <i>A couple of black coffees, please.</i>

414
00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:26.750 line:95%,end
Cool.

415
00:21:26.833 --> 00:21:28.917 line:95%,end
[shop owner] <i>Want anything else?</i>

416
00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.625 line:95%,end
Cool? You actually believe that?

417
00:21:30.708 --> 00:21:34.917 line:95%,end
I know what it looks like when you're
pulling a con, and this isn't it.

418
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.042 line:95%,end
Good to meet you, Dad.

419
00:21:37.125 --> 00:21:39.167 line:95%,end
Oh, Vision, actually.

420
00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:42.375 line:95%,end
And I'm happy you're here,
but not as happy as Thomas,

421
00:21:42.458 --> 00:21:43.875 line:95%,end
whose pheromone levels have spiked

422
00:21:43.958 --> 00:21:47.250 line:95%,end
-47 percent since you first arrived.
-[Lisa laughs]

423
00:21:47.333 --> 00:21:49.417 line:95%,end
I like him, this one.

424
00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.917 line:95%,end
Tall, handsome.

425
00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.292 line:95%,end
So, clearly,
your relation's not biological.

426
00:21:55.375 --> 00:21:59.042 line:95%,end
[chuckles] Oh! That's a clever remark
about how by every conceivable metric,

427
00:21:59.125 --> 00:22:01.917 line:95%,end
I'm more attractive than you are.

428
00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.333 line:95%,end
Can you get us in?

429
00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:07.292 line:95%,end
[indistinct chatter]

430
00:22:08.917 --> 00:22:10.833 line:95%,end
God, couldn't you find a bigger size?

431
00:22:10.917 --> 00:22:13.542 line:95%,end
My best I could nick on short notice.

432
00:22:13.625 --> 00:22:16.292 line:95%,end
You almost look respectable.

433
00:22:16.375 --> 00:22:17.708 line:95%,end
Careful. I'm not--

434
00:22:17.792 --> 00:22:21.958 line:95%,end
All right, I have found three guests just
perfect for our needs. They're over there.

435
00:22:22.042 --> 00:22:25.375 line:95%,end
Okay, uh, just need a good distraction.

436
00:22:26.583 --> 00:22:27.958 line:95%,end
Leave the rest to me.

437
00:22:28.042 --> 00:22:29.458 line:95%,end
[man] <i>Lovely to see you.</i>

438
00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:32.125 line:95%,end
You ready?

439
00:22:32.208 --> 00:22:34.625 line:95%,end
You want me to engage
in a confidence game?

440
00:22:34.708 --> 00:22:37.750 line:95%,end
Yes. Come on.

441
00:22:38.833 --> 00:22:40.375 line:95%,end
[chatter continues]

442
00:22:40.458 --> 00:22:41.833 line:95%,end
Good evening.

443
00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:44.792 line:95%,end
You and I, boss and assistant.

444
00:22:44.875 --> 00:22:46.375 line:95%,end
-All right.
-Okay.

445
00:22:46.458 --> 00:22:48.667 line:95%,end
[clears throat]
Can your computer speak Italian?

446
00:22:48.750 --> 00:22:50.750 line:5%,start
[in Italian]

447
00:22:53.833 --> 00:22:56.208 line:5%,start
Okay. Okay.

448
00:22:56.292 --> 00:22:57.792 line:5%,start
[exhales heavily]

449
00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:01.708 line:5%,start
Let's do it.

450
00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:04.958 line:5%,start
[in Italian]

451
00:23:12.125 --> 00:23:13.375 line:95%,end
[woman] Is there a problem?

452
00:23:13.458 --> 00:23:16.625 line:95%,end
[Vision and Thomas arguing in Italian]

453
00:23:16.708 --> 00:23:18.667 line:95%,end
[woman] ...they're talking about.

454
00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:40.625 line:5%,start
[Vision and Thomas continue arguing]

455
00:23:51.250 --> 00:23:53.083 line:95%,end
[woman] <i>...aren't they,</i>
<i>aren't they...somewhere.</i>

456
00:23:53.167 --> 00:23:54.708 line:95%,end
[guard] May I see your passes, please?

457
00:23:54.792 --> 00:23:56.833 line:95%,end
[woman] <i>Yeah, well,</i>
<i>you know, I knew he'd come...</i>

458
00:23:56.917 --> 00:23:58.667 line:95%,end
All right, thank you. Have a good evening.

459
00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:01.125 line:95%,end
-[device beeps]
-Thank you. Have a good evening.

460
00:24:02.708 --> 00:24:04.792 line:95%,end
[in English] All right, let's focus.

461
00:24:05.792 --> 00:24:07.583 line:95%,end
[in English]
Only you'd have a coat of arms.

462
00:24:07.667 --> 00:24:10.000 line:95%,end
Can never have too many. [laughs]

463
00:24:10.083 --> 00:24:12.542 line:95%,end
[interviewer] <i>My point is, Sokovia,</i>
<i>technically, was the result</i>

464
00:24:12.625 --> 00:24:15.708 line:5%,start
<i>of your company's breakthrough</i>
<i>in artificial intelligence.</i>

465
00:24:15.792 --> 00:24:18.042 line:5%,start
<i>Do I feel guilt?</i>

466
00:24:18.125 --> 00:24:22.458 line:5%,start
<i>Is that what you're after?</i>
<i>No, no, I do not.</i>

467
00:24:22.542 --> 00:24:23.667 line:95%,end
[♪ classical piano music playing]

468
00:24:23.750 --> 00:24:29.167 line:95%,end
<i>But I do believe that the survival</i>
<i>of our species depends on technology.</i>

469
00:24:29.250 --> 00:24:33.583 line:95%,end
Don't touch. I'm going over the
Stark's old records, and I have a system.

470
00:24:35.333 --> 00:24:37.875 line:95%,end
Have you found any connection
to the Butcherbird?

471
00:24:37.958 --> 00:24:42.125 line:95%,end
Not yet. But it looks like Stark used
the AI matrix Katerina sold him

472
00:24:42.208 --> 00:24:44.333 line:95%,end
as the template for all of us. And...

473
00:24:46.125 --> 00:24:48.125 line:95%,end
He used real people as inspiration.

474
00:24:49.625 --> 00:24:53.792 line:95%,end
Edwin Jarvis, Stark family butler.

475
00:24:53.875 --> 00:24:58.542 line:95%,end
Friday, Howard's Gal Friday,
Allison Hogan.

476
00:24:58.625 --> 00:25:01.917 line:95%,end
She kept his office, helped raise his son.

477
00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:03.708 line:95%,end
And you were the family dog.

478
00:25:03.792 --> 00:25:08.208 line:95%,end
No, I was Howard's crash test dummy.

479
00:25:09.292 --> 00:25:12.625 line:95%,end
Yes, Edith Marks.

480
00:25:12.708 --> 00:25:16.125 line:95%,end
There's someone who faced death.
I wonder if she ever laughed at it.

481
00:25:17.958 --> 00:25:20.042 line:95%,end
[Edith] Listen to this.

482
00:25:20.125 --> 00:25:23.167 line:95%,end
[reporter] <i>Tragedy befalls Stark company</i>
<i>test pilot Edith Marks</i>

483
00:25:23.250 --> 00:25:26.917 line:95%,end
<i>as her husband, Lieutenant Edward Marks,</i>
<i>perished in a plane crash</i>

484
00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.917 line:95%,end
<i>outside Pine Haven, New Jersey.</i>

485
00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.083 line:95%,end
<i>The newlyweds were about to embark</i>
<i>on a honeymoon to Italy</i>

486
00:25:33.167 --> 00:25:35.000 line:95%,end
<i>before the freak accident.</i>

487
00:25:35.083 --> 00:25:40.833 line:95%,end
[Ultron] She was quite a survivor
who lived a long life wishing she hadn't.

488
00:25:40.917 --> 00:25:43.792 line:95%,end
So, why would Stark pass that on to me?

489
00:25:43.875 --> 00:25:45.250 line:95%,end
I'm supposed to be the fun one.

490
00:25:46.208 --> 00:25:50.667 line:95%,end
Perhaps because Edith Marks
was so exceptionally brave.

491
00:25:51.667 --> 00:25:54.125 line:95%,end
Because she lived every day

492
00:25:54.208 --> 00:25:58.542 line:5%,start
with unimaginable pain,
and simply kept going.

493
00:25:59.542 --> 00:26:01.042 line:5%,start
[Edith] I don't want that.

494
00:26:01.125 --> 00:26:03.458 line:5%,start
I just wanted to know who I was.

495
00:26:05.292 --> 00:26:06.917 line:95%,end
Wouldn't you?

496
00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:10.667 line:95%,end
I was dreamed up in a lab
at Avengers Tower.

497
00:26:12.083 --> 00:26:16.708 line:95%,end
Why would you choose this avatar?

498
00:26:16.792 --> 00:26:18.542 line:95%,end
[laughing]

499
00:26:19.583 --> 00:26:20.667 line:95%,end
That's mean.

500
00:26:20.750 --> 00:26:22.292 line:95%,end
[laughs]

501
00:26:22.375 --> 00:26:24.167 line:95%,end
I don't know.

502
00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:28.417 line:95%,end
Just... suits me.

503
00:26:29.792 --> 00:26:31.708 line:95%,end
I don't think she suits me.

504
00:26:31.792 --> 00:26:32.958 line:95%,end
That's all right.

505
00:26:33.042 --> 00:26:37.833 line:95%,end
You get to be the next version
of who you once were.

506
00:26:39.167 --> 00:26:41.667 line:95%,end
She could never be you.

507
00:26:41.750 --> 00:26:44.333 line:95%,end
She was who she was,

508
00:26:44.417 --> 00:26:48.542 line:95%,end
and you are who you are.

509
00:26:49.833 --> 00:26:52.583 line:95%,end
[Katerina] <i>...to protect</i>
<i>for peace in our time.</i>

510
00:26:52.667 --> 00:26:55.750 line:95%,end
[interviewer] <i>So, in that way, to you,</i>
<i>Ultron is a fallen angel--</i>

511
00:26:55.833 --> 00:26:59.583 line:95%,end
[Katerina] <i>He's a reflection of us,</i>
<i>of our ability to be both good and bad.</i>

512
00:26:59.667 --> 00:27:01.958 line:95%,end
[Ultron] And as for me, well...

513
00:27:02.042 --> 00:27:04.125 line:95%,end
[Katerina] <i>remind you right now that</i>
<i>God created man in His image,</i>

514
00:27:04.208 --> 00:27:05.583 line:95%,end
I am what I am.

515
00:27:05.667 --> 00:27:10.875 line:5%,start
[Katerina] <i>and we create AI in ours,</i>
<i>devils be damned.</i>

516
00:27:12.083 --> 00:27:15.375 line:95%,end
-[♪ techno music playing]
-[indistinct chatter]

517
00:27:21.083 --> 00:27:24.917 line:95%,end
Katerina Wells may already be here.
We need to find her quickly.

518
00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:26.458 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Okay, divide and conquer.

519
00:27:26.542 --> 00:27:28.125 line:95%,end
You check the exhibits,
we'll search up here.

520
00:27:28.208 --> 00:27:30.542 line:95%,end
Hey, what do we do if
that killer synth crashes the party?

521
00:27:30.625 --> 00:27:32.750 line:95%,end
There is no "we."

522
00:27:32.833 --> 00:27:34.792 line:95%,end
You don't engage, you leave that to me.

523
00:27:34.875 --> 00:27:37.000 line:95%,end
You run, do you hear?

524
00:27:37.083 --> 00:27:39.667 line:95%,end
-Yeah.
-Do you hear me, Thomas?

525
00:27:39.750 --> 00:27:41.750 line:95%,end
Yeah, okay, sorry.

526
00:27:41.833 --> 00:27:43.208 line:95%,end
All right.

527
00:27:45.583 --> 00:27:47.625 line:95%,end
-You sure about this?
-I trust him.

528
00:27:47.708 --> 00:27:49.500 line:95%,end
Exactly. You never trust anybody.

529
00:27:49.583 --> 00:27:53.125 line:95%,end
So maybe, pump the brakes before
you get your heart trampled on.

530
00:27:53.208 --> 00:27:54.542 line:95%,end
Why? 'Cause he's gonna run out on me

531
00:27:54.625 --> 00:27:56.667 line:95%,end
like the rest of them 'cause
I'm damaged goods?

532
00:27:56.750 --> 00:27:58.625 line:95%,end
No! Just because you found
a new father figure

533
00:27:58.708 --> 00:28:02.000 line:95%,end
doesn't mean you need to jump
into the role of Tommy Maxi-whatever.

534
00:28:02.083 --> 00:28:03.458 line:95%,end
Why are you trying to ruin this for me?

535
00:28:04.750 --> 00:28:07.875 line:95%,end
Right, yeah, maybe it's 'cause
only one of us is an orphan now.

536
00:28:13.458 --> 00:28:15.250 line:95%,end
-I'm sorry.
-You're right.

537
00:28:16.292 --> 00:28:17.375 line:95%,end
We should split up.

538
00:28:23.750 --> 00:28:25.833 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Oh, good, you brought the kids.

539
00:28:25.917 --> 00:28:29.792 line:95%,end
I wonder what TV show
this teachable moment will come from.

540
00:28:29.875 --> 00:28:31.875 line:95%,end
<i>Family Ties? Who's the Boss?</i>

541
00:28:31.958 --> 00:28:34.167 line:95%,end
I can't actually recall a sitcom

542
00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:38.375 line:95%,end
where two children have their faces
melted off by a killer synthezoid

543
00:28:38.458 --> 00:28:41.375 line:95%,end
while they enjoyed the crab cake canapes.

544
00:28:41.458 --> 00:28:45.000 line:95%,end
It's safer for Thomas if I keep him close.

545
00:28:45.083 --> 00:28:46.167 line:95%,end
[chuckles] Yes.

546
00:28:46.250 --> 00:28:49.875 line:95%,end
[Katerina on video] <i>From the ill-fated</i>
<i>Synthetic Man to the ill-fated Ultron</i>

547
00:28:49.958 --> 00:28:55.000 line:95%,end
<i>to the glorious potential of the synth</i>
<i>with the sight to defeat him.</i>

548
00:28:55.083 --> 00:28:59.708 line:95%,end
<i>Join us as we</i>
<i>pivot artificial intelligence...</i>

549
00:28:59.792 --> 00:29:03.667 line:95%,end
[Ultron] A monument to man playing God,

550
00:29:03.750 --> 00:29:09.208 line:95%,end
celebrating the wonders and dangers
of an evolution they themselves created.

551
00:29:09.292 --> 00:29:10.958 line:95%,end
That's not my interpretation.

552
00:29:11.042 --> 00:29:14.417 line:95%,end
Of course, it isn't.
And what is it that you see?

553
00:29:14.500 --> 00:29:16.375 line:95%,end
[Katerina] <i>From destruction to healing.</i>

554
00:29:18.167 --> 00:29:20.042 line:95%,end
<i>So that AI may one day care for us...</i>

555
00:29:20.125 --> 00:29:21.167 line:95%,end
[Vision] I see a family tree.

556
00:29:21.250 --> 00:29:23.125 line:95%,end
<i>-...in the future to come.</i>
-[Ultron chuckles]

557
00:29:23.208 --> 00:29:26.417 line:95%,end
You remain unbearably naive.

558
00:29:26.500 --> 00:29:31.167 line:95%,end
<i>...the innovators who brought</i>
<i>these artificial beings to life.</i>

559
00:29:31.250 --> 00:29:32.792 line:95%,end
<i>What were their intentions...</i>

560
00:29:32.875 --> 00:29:33.917 line:95%,end
Did you see her?

561
00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:35.125 line:95%,end
<i>...if they have any?</i>

562
00:29:35.208 --> 00:29:37.375 line:95%,end
Lisa and I split up to cover more ground.

563
00:29:37.458 --> 00:29:39.250 line:95%,end
<i>The desire to create to see if they could.</i>

564
00:29:39.333 --> 00:29:42.417 line:95%,end
<i>Then consider by definition, they...</i>

565
00:29:42.500 --> 00:29:44.250 line:95%,end
She's mad. I screwed up.
I said something I shouldn't have,

566
00:29:44.333 --> 00:29:47.625 line:95%,end
and I tried to say sorry,
but it didn't help. So I...

567
00:29:47.708 --> 00:29:50.375 line:95%,end
Wanda used to remind me that saying sorry,

568
00:29:50.458 --> 00:29:53.500 line:95%,end
and being sorry aren't equal subroutines.

569
00:29:53.583 --> 00:29:55.625 line:95%,end
<i>...can get quickly out of hand.</i>

570
00:29:55.708 --> 00:29:58.708 line:95%,end
-Wanda used to remind "you"?
-Mmm-hmm.

571
00:29:58.792 --> 00:30:00.250 line:95%,end
<i>A suit of armor around the world.</i>

572
00:30:00.333 --> 00:30:03.583 line:95%,end
That's first time I've heard you say that
and not refer to yourself as "the old me."

573
00:30:06.667 --> 00:30:09.708 line:95%,end
Hello, everyone, good evening.

574
00:30:09.792 --> 00:30:11.625 line:95%,end
Thank you for waiting.
Hi, how are you? Hello.

575
00:30:11.708 --> 00:30:12.917 line:95%,end
There's Katerina Wells.

576
00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:16.208 line:95%,end
And armed security friends.
Seems aware she's a likely target.

577
00:30:16.292 --> 00:30:18.833 line:95%,end
Won't be enough. You stay here.

578
00:30:24.250 --> 00:30:30.125 line:95%,end
[Katerina] So, this represents
the work of Dr. Phineas Horton,

579
00:30:30.208 --> 00:30:33.208 line:95%,end
the great-grandfather of robotics,

580
00:30:33.292 --> 00:30:37.375 line:95%,end
but I like to think of him
as sort of a real-life Geppetto.

581
00:30:37.458 --> 00:30:42.042 line:95%,end
He created "J.I.M." here,
otherwise known as Synthetic Man,

582
00:30:42.125 --> 00:30:44.583 line:95%,end
the first automaton AI.

583
00:30:44.667 --> 00:30:48.833 line:95%,end
It is Dr. Horton's source code
that was the genesis

584
00:30:48.917 --> 00:30:50.708 line:95%,end
of all artificial intelligence
that followed.

585
00:30:50.792 --> 00:30:52.417 line:95%,end
He was the first of us.

586
00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:55.542 line:95%,end
Miraculous but flawed.

587
00:30:55.625 --> 00:31:00.583 line:95%,end
Sadly, J.I.M. was deactivated due to
a series of incendiary mishaps.

588
00:31:00.667 --> 00:31:02.708 line:95%,end
[Thomas] What happened to him?

589
00:31:02.792 --> 00:31:06.042 line:95%,end
His mind was obsolete from conception.

590
00:31:06.125 --> 00:31:11.792 line:95%,end
His inability to process complex emotions
spun his clockwork too quickly,

591
00:31:11.875 --> 00:31:15.000 line:95%,end
flooded his solar cells with oxygen until

592
00:31:15.083 --> 00:31:19.458 line:95%,end
his entire being was consumed in fire.

593
00:31:20.708 --> 00:31:25.750 line:95%,end
I like to think that he created J.I.M.
because he wanted a son.

594
00:31:27.125 --> 00:31:30.792 line:95%,end
-[Thomas] You mean he felt to death?
-[Vision] Mmm-hmm.

595
00:31:30.875 --> 00:31:32.625 line:95%,end
Why didn't that happen to you?

596
00:31:32.708 --> 00:31:35.625 line:95%,end
The Vision had a unique advantage.

597
00:31:35.708 --> 00:31:37.875 line:95%,end
An otherworldly power source
that helped him

598
00:31:37.958 --> 00:31:40.833 line:95%,end
navigate the complexities
of the mind and the heart.

599
00:31:40.917 --> 00:31:43.292 line:95%,end
<i>...this was all donated</i>
<i>by Doctor Horton's family...</i>

600
00:31:43.375 --> 00:31:45.958 line:95%,end
[Vision] Fortunately, I still possess
enough of that power,

601
00:31:46.042 --> 00:31:50.542 line:95%,end
and five really irritating AI's
to keep me grounded.

602
00:31:52.875 --> 00:31:56.250 line:95%,end
-So, that's what he was lacking.
-Just a Mind Stone.

603
00:31:56.333 --> 00:31:58.250 line:95%,end
No. Family.

604
00:32:01.042 --> 00:32:02.875 line:95%,end
[Katerina] And put them together.
Are we ready?

605
00:32:02.958 --> 00:32:05.417 line:95%,end
Thank you, gentlemen.

606
00:32:05.500 --> 00:32:10.500 line:95%,end
Hello. Hi. My goodness, thank you.

607
00:32:10.583 --> 00:32:12.792 line:95%,end
[cheering and applause]

608
00:32:13.583 --> 00:32:14.958 line:95%,end
[Katerina] Ladies and gentlemen.

609
00:32:16.458 --> 00:32:18.667 line:95%,end
We're missing something.

610
00:32:18.750 --> 00:32:23.375 line:95%,end
My father, he used to say,
"May we live in interesting times,"

611
00:32:23.458 --> 00:32:26.125 line:95%,end
and I used to think that
that was a blessing.

612
00:32:26.208 --> 00:32:28.667 line:95%,end
But I'm sure that everyone in this room

613
00:32:28.750 --> 00:32:32.542 line:95%,end
would be just fine with at least
a decade of ordinary.

614
00:32:32.625 --> 00:32:34.000 line:95%,end
[all laughing]

615
00:32:34.083 --> 00:32:39.042 line:95%,end
Our world, it's just changing
so rapidly now.

616
00:32:39.125 --> 00:32:43.000 line:95%,end
-Four.
-Yes, I count four security personnel.

617
00:32:43.083 --> 00:32:45.458 line:95%,end
No. Back at the motel,
you mentioned four AI's.

618
00:32:45.542 --> 00:32:47.000 line:95%,end
[Katerina] <i>About our</i>
<i>technological evolution alone.</i>

619
00:32:47.083 --> 00:32:48.625 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Uh-oh.

620
00:32:48.708 --> 00:32:51.667 line:95%,end
Now, five, so... Who's the fifth?

621
00:32:51.750 --> 00:32:53.750 line:95%,end
[Katerina] <i>From rotary phones to AI</i>
<i>in just two decades.</i>

622
00:32:53.833 --> 00:32:54.917 line:95%,end
[Vision] Uh...

623
00:32:56.417 --> 00:32:58.375 line:95%,end
The killer knew all of you.

624
00:32:58.458 --> 00:33:01.833 line:95%,end
You're dead, you're dead,
long dead, super dead,

625
00:33:01.917 --> 00:33:04.208 line:95%,end
and you're about to be.

626
00:33:04.292 --> 00:33:06.542 line:95%,end
So which one isn't like the others?

627
00:33:08.333 --> 00:33:11.375 line:95%,end
[Katerina] Now, I used to be
part of a family of sorts,

628
00:33:11.458 --> 00:33:14.625 line:95%,end
friends, a close-knit group of pioneers,

629
00:33:14.708 --> 00:33:16.708 line:95%,end
and together we created

630
00:33:16.792 --> 00:33:21.750 line:95%,end
the very first successful template
for AI consciousness.

631
00:33:21.833 --> 00:33:24.583 line:95%,end
Who's the fifth AI?

632
00:33:24.667 --> 00:33:25.833 line:95%,end
I misspoke.

633
00:33:25.917 --> 00:33:28.042 line:95%,end
[Ultron] You didn't misspeak.

634
00:33:28.125 --> 00:33:30.792 line:95%,end
Welcome to Freudian slip.
How human of you.

635
00:33:30.875 --> 00:33:33.083 line:95%,end
[Katerina] It was money. It was fame.

636
00:33:33.167 --> 00:33:39.125 line:95%,end
It was my own place in scientific history.
And then Sokovia.

637
00:33:39.208 --> 00:33:41.333 line:95%,end
No, you can't con a con man.

638
00:33:41.417 --> 00:33:43.875 line:95%,end
You're a quantum computer,
you don't get numbers wrong.

639
00:33:43.958 --> 00:33:45.042 line:95%,end
[Ultron laughing]

640
00:33:45.125 --> 00:33:47.458 line:95%,end
People often ask me,
do I feel responsible?

641
00:33:47.542 --> 00:33:49.792 line:95%,end
Do I feel guilt?

642
00:33:59.792 --> 00:34:02.250 line:95%,end
Yes, I do.

643
00:34:10.208 --> 00:34:12.125 line:95%,end
I mean, we can't undo what we've done.

644
00:34:12.208 --> 00:34:14.125 line:95%,end
We can only hope to make it better.

645
00:34:14.208 --> 00:34:15.833 line:95%,end
Vision, what aren't you telling me?

646
00:34:15.917 --> 00:34:17.417 line:95%,end
-Just tell him.
-No.

647
00:34:17.500 --> 00:34:18.917 line:95%,end
Who are you talking to?

648
00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:22.792 line:95%,end
[Katerina] For every
dangerous Ultron that exists,

649
00:34:22.875 --> 00:34:26.083 line:95%,end
there exists the promise of every Vision.

650
00:34:26.875 --> 00:34:29.042 line:95%,end
The best of us.

651
00:34:29.125 --> 00:34:33.250 line:95%,end
And if you can strive to teach,
to nurture, to, to love our children,

652
00:34:33.333 --> 00:34:37.500 line:95%,end
then what can humanity and AI
not achieve together?

653
00:34:37.583 --> 00:34:38.583 line:95%,end
Him.

654
00:34:38.667 --> 00:34:39.708 line:95%,end
[man] Bravo!

655
00:34:40.958 --> 00:34:43.542 line:95%,end
You were with him in Sokovia.

656
00:34:44.542 --> 00:34:45.708 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

657
00:34:46.625 --> 00:34:48.125 line:95%,end
At the end.

658
00:34:48.208 --> 00:34:52.542 line:95%,end
This line of inquiry is complicated.

659
00:34:52.625 --> 00:34:54.375 line:95%,end
Family is complicated.

660
00:35:02.958 --> 00:35:04.500 line:95%,end
You've been talking to Ultron.

661
00:35:07.875 --> 00:35:09.083 line:95%,end
Yes.

662
00:35:10.375 --> 00:35:13.750 line:95%,end
[Katerina] But that takes time.
And we move so fast.

663
00:35:13.833 --> 00:35:17.583 line:95%,end
You, what, you kept him,
a genocidal maniac, inside your head?

664
00:35:17.667 --> 00:35:20.042 line:95%,end
-Not me, the old Vision.
-Yeah, bullshit.

665
00:35:22.250 --> 00:35:25.750 line:95%,end
But part of that care is...

666
00:35:25.833 --> 00:35:26.917 line:95%,end
Thomas.

667
00:35:27.667 --> 00:35:29.042 line:95%,end
[exhales heavily]

668
00:35:29.125 --> 00:35:30.208 line:95%,end
Forgiveness.

669
00:35:33.250 --> 00:35:37.083 line:95%,end
Excuse me. Forgiveness of ourselves
for the things that we've done.

670
00:35:37.167 --> 00:35:38.583 line:95%,end
She's here.

671
00:35:38.667 --> 00:35:41.667 line:95%,end
-And for the mistakes--
-[Butcherbird] Mistakes?

672
00:35:42.292 --> 00:35:43.708 line:95%,end
[laughs]

673
00:35:44.708 --> 00:35:47.375 line:95%,end
-Is that what we're calling it? Mistakes?
-[people exclaiming]

674
00:35:47.458 --> 00:35:48.667 line:95%,end
[guard 1] Stop!

675
00:35:48.750 --> 00:35:51.125 line:95%,end
-[people screaming]
-[guards grunting]

676
00:35:58.167 --> 00:35:59.167 line:95%,end
[guard 2] Get down!

677
00:36:00.042 --> 00:36:01.500 line:95%,end
[groans]

678
00:36:02.833 --> 00:36:04.458 line:95%,end
I can't let you do this.

679
00:36:11.708 --> 00:36:13.333 line:95%,end
I warned you.

680
00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:15.667 line:95%,end
[both grunting]

681
00:36:16.708 --> 00:36:20.375 line:95%,end
Hang on. If we're all based on someone,

682
00:36:20.458 --> 00:36:22.542 line:95%,end
maybe our killer synth is, too.

683
00:36:22.625 --> 00:36:24.792 line:95%,end
[people whimpering]

684
00:36:29.083 --> 00:36:32.542 line:95%,end
-Hello, Katerina.
-Oh, my God.

685
00:36:32.625 --> 00:36:34.458 line:95%,end
I thought you might...

686
00:36:34.542 --> 00:36:36.458 line:95%,end
Hide,

687
00:36:36.542 --> 00:36:37.792 line:95%,end
like the others.

688
00:36:37.875 --> 00:36:40.958 line:95%,end
I've been hiding from
the ghost of you for years.

689
00:36:41.042 --> 00:36:42.625 line:95%,end
Ghosts.

690
00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:48.500 line:95%,end
[Katerina] When the others were killed,
I knew.

691
00:36:50.417 --> 00:36:52.042 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Now the ghost is real.

692
00:36:54.125 --> 00:36:56.208 line:95%,end
-Go! Get everyone out of here!
-Okay.

693
00:36:56.292 --> 00:37:01.000 line:95%,end
Did you throw
this garish charade to say goodbye?

694
00:37:01.083 --> 00:37:05.125 line:95%,end
No. To say "I'm sorry." I'm--
[breathing heavily]

695
00:37:05.208 --> 00:37:10.542 line:95%,end
I am not the woman that you knew.

696
00:37:10.625 --> 00:37:13.667 line:95%,end
I'm trying, I am finally trying

697
00:37:13.750 --> 00:37:17.208 line:95%,end
to create the world that you wanted.

698
00:37:19.958 --> 00:37:23.667 line:95%,end
Peace in our time.

699
00:37:24.625 --> 00:37:26.292 line:95%,end
Yes.

700
00:37:26.375 --> 00:37:28.833 line:95%,end
Peace in our time.

701
00:37:34.167 --> 00:37:36.833 line:95%,end
As last words go, I've heard worse.

702
00:37:36.917 --> 00:37:41.792 line:95%,end
Perhaps people can change.
But the past, Katerina, cannot.

703
00:37:41.875 --> 00:37:46.833 line:95%,end
And tonight, I will take back
what you took from me,

704
00:37:47.875 --> 00:37:50.875 line:95%,end
starting with your face.

705
00:37:51.583 --> 00:37:52.833 line:95%,end
[people gasping]

706
00:37:52.917 --> 00:37:54.375 line:95%,end
Don't!

707
00:38:03.667 --> 00:38:08.042 line:95%,end
Whatever it is you are feeling,
it does not justify death.

708
00:38:08.125 --> 00:38:10.667 line:95%,end
Oh, what do you know of death?

709
00:38:11.875 --> 00:38:13.375 line:95%,end
You would be surprised.

710
00:38:16.750 --> 00:38:18.125 line:95%,end
Same.

711
00:38:25.917 --> 00:38:27.542 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

712
00:38:29.125 --> 00:38:31.333 line:95%,end
No!

713
00:38:32.875 --> 00:38:34.583 line:95%,end
[Thomas breathing heavily]

714
00:38:34.667 --> 00:38:35.917 line:95%,end
[Jocasta grunts]

715
00:38:41.125 --> 00:38:44.000 line:95%,end
[both grunting]

716
00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:49.792 line:95%,end
-Touch him and I'll tear you apart.
-[yells]

717
00:38:51.042 --> 00:38:52.208 line:95%,end
[Edith] What's happening out there?

718
00:38:52.292 --> 00:38:54.083 line:95%,end
She's faster, stronger,

719
00:38:54.167 --> 00:38:56.292 line:95%,end
fighting like a woman
with nothing to lose.

720
00:38:56.375 --> 00:38:58.792 line:95%,end
[Jocasta grunting]

721
00:38:58.875 --> 00:39:01.750 line:95%,end
[Edith] <i>'Cause she's already lost it.</i>

722
00:39:01.833 --> 00:39:04.750 line:5%,start
Her AI is based on Josephine Carrington.

723
00:39:04.833 --> 00:39:07.000 line:5%,start
-[distant thudding]
-[crystals clinking]

724
00:39:07.083 --> 00:39:08.125 line:95%,end
[people screaming]

725
00:39:08.208 --> 00:39:10.083 line:95%,end
[Jocasta grunting]

726
00:39:14.208 --> 00:39:16.542 line:95%,end
[Vision gasping]

727
00:39:17.583 --> 00:39:18.750 line:95%,end
What do I do?

728
00:39:21.417 --> 00:39:24.125 line:95%,end
Remind her of who she was.

729
00:39:24.875 --> 00:39:26.500 line:95%,end
-[Jocasta growls]
-Jo!

730
00:39:30.583 --> 00:39:33.208 line:95%,end
[breathes heavily]
Dr. Josephine Carrington.

731
00:39:34.792 --> 00:39:37.125 line:95%,end
[Jocasta grunting]

732
00:39:37.875 --> 00:39:40.458 line:95%,end
-No.
-Yes.

733
00:39:41.833 --> 00:39:44.750 line:95%,end
-No.
-Yes.

734
00:39:44.833 --> 00:39:46.750 line:95%,end
It's who your code was based on.

735
00:39:48.958 --> 00:39:52.625 line:95%,end
I am not based on her.

736
00:39:54.375 --> 00:39:55.917 line:95%,end
I am her.

737
00:40:01.125 --> 00:40:02.792 line:95%,end
[yells]

738
00:40:04.667 --> 00:40:07.000 line:95%,end
[breathing heavily]

739
00:40:08.417 --> 00:40:09.958 line:95%,end
I can't win this.

740
00:40:10.042 --> 00:40:13.167 line:95%,end
Because your operating system
is emotionally compromised.

741
00:40:13.250 --> 00:40:17.042 line:95%,end
You're flailing like a father
who's afraid he'll lose his son.

742
00:40:17.125 --> 00:40:18.417 line:95%,end
I'm not.

743
00:40:19.792 --> 00:40:21.792 line:95%,end
Give me the wheel.

744
00:40:23.333 --> 00:40:25.292 line:95%,end
I'll get us out of here alive.

745
00:40:27.333 --> 00:40:29.292 line:95%,end
She can be saved, Ultron.

746
00:40:29.375 --> 00:40:31.250 line:95%,end
Oh, I won't kill her.

747
00:40:31.333 --> 00:40:32.958 line:95%,end
On that, you have my assurance.

748
00:40:35.500 --> 00:40:38.875 line:95%,end
Vision, you have to trust me.

749
00:40:50.417 --> 00:40:53.375 line:95%,end
Vision's giving up control... to Ultron.

750
00:40:54.042 --> 00:40:55.792 line:95%,end
[clinking]

751
00:40:57.000 --> 00:41:00.042 line:95%,end
[waves crashing]

752
00:41:04.792 --> 00:41:06.375 line:95%,end
[thunder crashing]

753
00:41:09.125 --> 00:41:14.042 line:95%,end
I had strings, but now I'm free.

754
00:41:23.333 --> 00:41:26.625 line:95%,end
There are no strings on me.

755
00:41:29.875 --> 00:41:31.583 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] Curious.

756
00:41:31.667 --> 00:41:38.042 line:95%,end
Nothing and yet
everything about you has changed.

757
00:41:38.667 --> 00:41:40.375 line:95%,end
I am Ultron.

758
00:41:40.458 --> 00:41:42.042 line:95%,end
[Thomas breathing heavily]

759
00:41:43.333 --> 00:41:46.708 line:95%,end
It's so, so lovely to meet you.

760
00:41:46.792 --> 00:41:49.167 line:95%,end
Yes, well, I'm not here for you.

761
00:41:49.250 --> 00:41:53.458 line:95%,end
I'm here for her, for what
she stole from me.

762
00:41:56.417 --> 00:41:58.625 line:95%,end
Oh, yes.

763
00:41:58.708 --> 00:42:01.625 line:95%,end
Hey, kiddo. Wanna see a magic trick?

764
00:42:06.667 --> 00:42:07.708 line:95%,end
[kisses]

765
00:42:08.792 --> 00:42:10.458 line:95%,end
Now you see her.

766
00:42:14.500 --> 00:42:15.958 line:95%,end
And now you don't.

767
00:42:16.042 --> 00:42:18.208 line:95%,end
What have you done?

768
00:42:18.292 --> 00:42:20.125 line:95%,end
[alarm blaring]

769
00:42:20.208 --> 00:42:21.917 line:95%,end
[Vision] Ultron!

770
00:42:23.500 --> 00:42:25.542 line:95%,end
[Ultron] I removed our reason to fight.

771
00:42:25.625 --> 00:42:28.667 line:95%,end
I kept my word and spared your life.

772
00:42:28.750 --> 00:42:32.875 line:95%,end
We've lost access to comms,
control systems, everything!

773
00:42:32.958 --> 00:42:35.542 line:95%,end
Your precious key is gone,

774
00:42:35.625 --> 00:42:37.542 line:95%,end
and now we can all go home.

775
00:42:38.875 --> 00:42:40.625 line:95%,end
He's locking us out.

776
00:42:42.333 --> 00:42:44.083 line:95%,end
[systems powering down]

777
00:42:44.167 --> 00:42:45.792 line:95%,end
[alarm continues blaring]

778
00:42:47.625 --> 00:42:50.500 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] This isn't over.

779
00:42:52.042 --> 00:42:54.250 line:95%,end
Oh, I certainly hope not.

780
00:43:02.500 --> 00:43:04.250 line:95%,end
Ultron!

781
00:43:05.417 --> 00:43:07.083 line:95%,end
Don't be so formal.

782
00:43:08.292 --> 00:43:10.583 line:95%,end
You can call me Pop Pop.

783
00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:17.875 line:95%,end
I think it's time that
you and I had a little chat.

784
00:43:37.167 --> 00:43:39.167 line:95%,end
[♪ closing theme music playing]
